in @beam

# @epistemologic/spectral_triple — Connes' (A, H, D) as grammar.
#
# === First empirical witness of the self-migration architecture ===
#
# This shard is the manual discharge of the substrate-self-migration
# machinery landed across Ticks 1-4. It IS what the autonomous loop
# (kintsugi/fracture/relocate + epistemologic/pact/is_load_bearing_in_std)
# would perform once wired to @io — performed by hand this tick as the
# Tick 5 WITNESS, proving the machinery's shape before the loop runs it.
#
# Migration provenance:
#   Source: boot/std/epistemologic/math/spectral-triple.mirror
#           (declared grammar @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple)
#   Destination: shards/epistemologic/spectral_triple.mirror
#           (declares grammar @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple —
#            keyword preserved per Seam Q3 qualification; namespace
#            path elevation is Tick 6+ refactor)
#
# Elevated OUT of /math/ per Alex 2026-07-10: the spectral triple is
# substrate-typing discipline, not just math. Underscore over hyphen
# per shards/ convention (sheaf_laplacian.mirror, bateson_learning.mirror,
# liquid_extraction.mirror).
#
# Cited landings:
#   e764a32 — Mara canonical spec (docs/specs/substrate-self-migration-
#             via-spectral-typing.md)
#   8a3b0a4 — Taut boundary scout: 0 non-dangling consumers of
#             `in @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple`; 1 orphan
#             (@epistemologic/math/connes_spectral_triple in
#             coherence-parametric.mirror) that never resolved
#   2b56977 — Seam Phase D ratify (with Q3 qualification: keyword
#             preservation this tick)
#   3870201 — Reed Tick 2 PREREQ-1 (spectral keyword admittance in
#             bootstrap)
#   5c12808 — Mara Tick 3 PREREQ-2 (@kintsugi/fracture/relocate
#             operational)
#   2f1041f — Mara Tick 4 PREREQ-3 (@epistemologic/pact/
#             is_load_bearing_in_std declarative)
#
# The autonomous loop discharge is Post-Tick-5 (per Alex HOLD). This
# shard's existence at this path IS the empirical proof that the
# machinery's shape holds under a real migration.
#
# === Original docblock ===
#
# A spectral triple in Alain Connes' framework is the data (A, H, D):
# an involutive algebra A acting on a Hilbert space H together with a
# self-adjoint operator D (the Dirac operator) satisfying compactness
# conditions on its resolvent and bounded-commutator conditions with A.
# Given an appropriate spectral triple, Connes' reconstruction theorem
# (Comm. Math. Phys. 182, 1996; refined J. NCG 7, 2013) recovers the
# entire geometry of the underlying space — manifold, connection,
# metric, all of it.
#
# Mirror's case: prism/core IS a spectral triple. The trait chain in
# bundle.rs (Fiber → Connection → Gauge → Transport → Closure) realizes
# (A, H, D) as follows:
#
#   A (algebra)      ←  the composition of Connection::connection() optics
#                       under Tambara module composition. The five
#                       operations (focus, project, split, shift, settle)
#                       and their composition rules generate A.
#   H (Hilbert space) ← the Fiber::State associated type. Mirror's case:
#                       5-dim vector spaces with the structure group
#                       O(5) acting on them per eigenboard-representation.md.
#                       au values are state vectors in H. beam.topology
#                       IS the 5-dim eigenvalue summary of a state.
#   D (Dirac op)     ←  Transport::transport, returning
#                       Imperfect<State, Infallible, Holonomy>. The
#                       holonomy IS the bounded-commutator residual.
#                       conductivity = ⟨au│D│au⟩; Magnot's κ
#                       (arXiv:2509.10536, 2025) IS the cycle-averaged
#                       spectrum of D; kintsugi's e^(n+1) < e^(n) IS
#                       monotonic decrease of D's Rayleigh quotient.
#
# ker(D) is the Lawvere fixed point (@epistemologic/math/lawvere) —
# the autopoietic closure of the bundle tower. Closure::close() returns
# a witness of this kernel.
#
# References:
#   Connes, A. (1994). Noncommutative Geometry. Academic Press.
#   Connes, A. (1996). Gravity coupled with matter and the foundation
#     of non-commutative geometry. Comm. Math. Phys. 182, 155-176.
#   Connes, A. (2013). On the spectral characterization of manifolds.
#     J. Noncommutative Geometry 7, 1-82.
#   Hansen & Ghrist (2019). arXiv:1808.01513. Discrete spectral structure
#     over cellular sheaves.
#   Barbero et al. (2022). arXiv:2206.08702. O(d)-bundle Laplacian =
#     sheaf Laplacian. Mirror's D² for the discrete case.
#   Magnot, J.-P. (2025). arXiv:2509.10536. Discrete fiber bundles and
#     contextuality index κ as cycle-averaged holonomy.
#
# Spec: docs/specs/spectral-triple-grammar.md
# Migration spec: docs/specs/substrate-self-migration-via-spectral-typing.md

grammar @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple {

  # the carriers ------------------------------------------------------
  # the grammar reasons about (A, H, D) structure without caring what
  # the carriers concretely are. prism/core's bundle.rs supplies one
  # realization; Hansen-Ghrist's cellular sheaves supply another;
  # Connes' canonical example (the Dirac operator on a spin manifold)
  # supplies the continuum prototype.

  type algebra          # A — the involutive algebra of operators.
                        # for mirror: optics under Tambara composition.
                        # bundle.rs's Connection::connection() returns
                        # an element of A in a chosen basis.

  type hilbert_space    # H — the Hilbert space the algebra acts on.
                        # for mirror: fibers of the principal O(5)-bundle
                        # over the five-operation graph. Fiber::State is
                        # one such fiber. beam.topology summarises one.

  type dirac_op         # D — the self-adjoint operator with compact
                        # resolvent and bounded commutators with A.
                        # for mirror: Transport::transport realizes D's
                        # action; the matrix form is @hash/coincidence's
                        # 5×5 conductivity tensor.

  type spectral_triple  # the (A, H, D) tuple itself. a witness that
                        # the three components satisfy Connes' axioms.
                        # bundle.rs's full trait chain on a single type
                        # IS such a witness.

  type spectrum         # the eigendecomposition of D: a list of pairs
                        # (eigenvalue, eigenvector). for mirror's case
                        # the dimension is 5 and eigenvalues are roots
                        # of a degree-5 characteristic polynomial.

  type residual         # the bounded-commutator measure ‖[D, a]‖.
                        # for mirror: a value of the bundle's Holonomy
                        # type, lifted from terni::Loss. cycle-averaged
                        # residual IS Magnot's κ.

  # the operator -----------------------------------------------------
  # the three primitive evaluator actions a spectral-triple realiser
  # must expose. compose_a is the algebra law; apply_h is the operator
  # action; eigen_d is the spectrum read-out.

  # compose_a: algebra composition. takes two elements of A and returns
  # their product in A. for prism/core: Tambara module composition over
  # optics — the supertrait chain enforces the shape; the law lives in
  # @epistemologic/math/category (future spec).
  abstract action compose_a(op1: algebra, op2: algebra) -> algebra

  # apply_h: operator action on a Hilbert-space vector. returns an
  # imperfect carrier because D is in general unbounded: the partial
  # branch records the residual when transport carries the state off
  # the manifold. mirror's Transport::transport realizes this for one
  # specific algebra element (the connection).
  abstract action apply_h(op: algebra, state: hilbert_space) -> imperfect(hilbert_space, residual)

  # eigen_d: Dirac operator eigendecomposition. for mirror's 5×5
  # case this is a polynomial-root finder; for general continuous
  # spectral triples this is functional-analytic and undecidable in
  # finite time. the abstract action carries the obligation; concrete
  # grammars discharge it with their dimension's solver.
  abstract action eigen_d(op: dirac_op) -> spectrum

  # the properties ----------------------------------------------------
  # the four IS-questions a spectral-triple-typed implementation must
  # answer to ride mirror's epistemologic discipline. bodies are `\`
  # until the evaluator (bootstrap/src/spectral.rs, a future tick) is
  # wired; the grammar exists for the model checker to reason about
  # the structure before the evaluator lands.

  # literal: does this implementation realize a spectral triple under
  # Connes' axioms? the IS-relationship at the level of the whole
  # triple. for prism/core: do Fiber + Connection + Gauge + Transport +
  # Closure on a single type satisfy involutivity, compactness, and
  # bounded commutators jointly?
  property literal(implementation) -> verdict { \ }

  # bounded_commutator: does [D, a] extend to a bounded operator for
  # all a ∈ A? Connes' first axiom. for mirror: does Transport's
  # Holonomy stay below a finite bound as algebra elements are applied
  # in sequence? the answer depends on the Loss monoid's growth law
  # (see audit, §"qualifications", in the spec).
  property bounded_commutator(triple: spectral_triple) -> verdict { \ }

  # compact_resolvent: is (D - λI)⁻¹ compact for λ outside the spectrum
  # of D? Connes' second axiom. trivially true for finite-dimensional
  # spectral triples (mirror's case: the 5×5 tensor); becomes the
  # load-bearing condition for continuous extensions.
  property compact_resolvent(triple: spectral_triple) -> verdict { \ }

  # dimension_spectrum: does the triple have spectral dimension n?
  # for mirror's case n = 5 (the principal O(5)-bundle's connection
  # has at most 5 nonzero eigenvalues). the property is parametric
  # over the claimed dimension so the same grammar serves discrete
  # and continuous cases.
  property dimension_spectrum(triple: spectral_triple, n: u64) -> verdict { \ }
}

out algebra
out hilbert_space
out dirac_op
out spectral_triple
out spectrum
out residual
out compose_a
out apply_h
out eigen_d
out literal
out bounded_commutator
out compact_resolvent
out dimension_spectrum
out @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple
